z3u = z1z + tools/ledger.py + KING_CALL (new switch; ledgered hooks in King.turn and twice in Baby.turn, G.settle
K 18). At war a king squeaks (SQ_RING) its centre and a 16-bit mask of the ring tiles at Chebyshev 2 that hold enemy
babies (touching its 3x3 body, so able to bite it). A baby with its action and turn ready, within Chebyshev 3 of a
king, that stands beside one of those tiles but cannot see it turns to it and bites. Babies only turn and bite: no
movement changes (GUARD_KING_R, rejected 4 times, and KING_EYES u7q moved defenders).
Evidence (scratch kguard2.py over the 73 cached replica matches, positions as of each robot's turn, enemies our
rats carry excluded; corrected 16:32 from kguard.py's end-of-round count, which counted carried enemies): a baby of
ours stood beside a free enemy baby on our king's ring 2,022 times and bit it 168 times. 348 of those turns ended
blind (outside the 90-degree cone) with the action and turn unused, 253 more blind with the turn used; at most 31 a
game (corridorofdoom A vs Varun), 12 in thunderdome A vs Varun (18346 g2), where 2-4 biters took our king from 354
to 0 in r230-436 while 14-24 of ours stood within Chebyshev 4. The ceiling is small: about 600 extra bites over
the corpus. Debug copy bots/zkc (untracked) confirmed the path: on DefaultMedium A vs araid the king's squeak reached
the babies the same round and 3 of 4 adjacent blind cases ended in a bite.

Falsifiers, registered before any z3u game:
1. Screen zd168 (vs zd136) on the s6 gates: t <= -1.5, picks z <= -2, transfer per round < 0.97x, any overrun.
2. Mechanism: in z3u's screen and check games, KING_CALL bites (bites by our babies on enemies they could not see at
   the turn's start, at ring tiles) must be at least 3x z1z's adjacent bites on king-biters in the same cells; and in
   games where both lose the king, z3u's king must not die earlier on average. Fewer, or an earlier death, drops it.
3. Replica: block rules against the twin; on set 3, enemy bite rounds on our king that pass with a baby of ours
   adjacent and unbitten must fall by half against z3q's block (kguard.py), or the mechanism did not transfer.
